      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Ordinal numbers show order or rank. They're used a lot for events that happen regularly: anniversaries, editions, festivals, birthdays of an institution."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Number",
            "Ordinal"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "11th",
              "undécimo / decimoprimero"
            ],
            [
              "12th",
              "duodécimo / decimosegundo"
            ],
            [
              "13th",
              "decimotercero"
            ],
            [
              "15th",
              "decimoquinto"
            ],
            [
              "20th",
              "vigésimo"
            ],
            [
              "21st",
              "vigésimo primero / vigesimoprimero"
            ],
            [
              "25th",
              "vigésimo quinto"
            ],
            [
              "30th",
              "trigésimo"
            ],
            [
              "40th",
              "cuadragésimo"
            ],
            [
              "50th",
              "quincuagésimo"
            ],
            [
              "100th",
              "centésimo"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "They **agree** in gender and number: **el vigésimo aniversario**, **la vigésima edición**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Primero** and **tercero** shorten before a masculine noun: **el vigésimo primer aniversario**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In everyday speech, after **décimo**, many people use cardinal numbers instead: **el aniversario veinte**, **la edición quince**. The ordinals sound more formal."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **-ésimo** is the ending of big birthdays: **vigésimo**, **trigésimo**, **centésimo**."
        }
      ]
    },
